# Hollyland wireless-mic USB-C receiver dongle (3547:0407, model 6108).
# Evidence: inputs/lsusb-v.txt [descriptor], docs/device.md.
#
# Grants the active seat user access to the usbfs device node (logind ACL)
# so holly-usb (nusb) can claim IF0 (the HID control interface) without
# sudo. IF1/IF2 (UAC audio) share the same node — but claiming is
# per-interface, so this rule does not enable claiming them.
#
# FILE NAME MUST BE <= 73: the uaccess BUILTIN is invoked by systemd's
# 73-seat-late.rules — verbatim from systemd main (2026-11-05):
#     TAG=="uaccess|xaccess-*", ENV{MAJOR}!="", RUN{builtin}+="uaccess"
# Rules run in lexical order, so a TAG+="uaccess" set in a 99- file is
# assigned AFTER that runner has already skipped TAG=="uaccess" and gone
# to its end label. Observed live 2026-11-05 (then-named 99-hollyland.rules):
# TAGS in the udev database did gain ':uaccess:seat:' and MODE applied, but
# the node never received the user's ACL — while the same builtin worked
# for /dev/snd nodes (their uaccess tag comes from 70-uaccess.rules, a
# runner-visible order). File renamed to 70- to make the tag runner-visible;
# treat the live effect as CONFIRMED-in-source / NOT-YET-confirmed-on-device
# until the replug getfacl check passes.
#
# Install (this also removes the earlier 99- name!):
#   sudo rm -f /etc/udev/rules.d/99-hollyland.rules
#   sudo cp packaging/70-hollyland.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload
#   sudo udevadm trigger --action=add /sys/bus/usb/devices/<sysfs-node>
#       (or unplug/replug — the trigger just avoids the replug)
# Verify: getfacl /dev/bus/usb/<bus>/<dev>  → expect user:<you>:rw- + mask

SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="3547", ATTR{idProduct}=="0407", TAG+="uaccess", MODE="0660"
